# Klenovica cemetery, photographed 29 September 2026.
#
# cemetery: Klenovica cemetery
# photographed: 29 September 2026
#
# One plaque, not a survey. David was travelling through Klenovica, stopped at
# a grave, and sent a photograph in chat -- this is that one plaque, not a
# walk of the churchyard the way Otocac and Senj were done.
#
# WHAT IT IS. A marble plaque reading OBITELJ PAPIC ("the Papic family"),
# carrying three names, mounted on -- or against -- a much larger STIPANIC
# family monument. Whether that placement means a Papic married into the
# Stipanic family, or the two plots simply share a wall, is not established
# and is not guessed at here.
#
# NONE OF THE THREE MATCH THE TREE, AND NONE MATCH SENJ'S MILKA PAPIC EITHER.
# This archive's only prior Papic cemetery evidence is Senj
# (sources/graves/senj-2024-10-09.psv), where a Milka Papic -- ahnentafel 3,
# carved under her married name as "MILKA BLAZEVIC rod. PAPIC", 1886-1971 --
# is already read at full resolution. This plaque's Milka has different years
# under any reading. Same given name, same surname, not the same woman, and
# not (yet) the same family: no Papic in this tree is tied to Klenovica at
# all, so this is a new place for the surname rather than a new fact about a
# line already held.
#
# READ ON SITE, NOT FROM A PHOTOGRAPH THIS ARCHIVE ENLARGED. David read the
# worn digits by eye, standing in front of the stone, rather than this archive
# cropping and re-reading a photograph -- a different kind of evidence from
# Otocac and Senj's own "r" rows, better than a guess, short of a full-
# resolution pass this archive made itself.
#
# "conf" is how the reading was made:
#   r = read at FULL RESOLUTION, cropped and enlarged 3-8x by this archive
#   p = read on site by eye, or from a photograph at reduced scale; the name
#       is secure and one confident year-pair was given, but not independently
#       verified by this archive against a full-resolution image
#   ? = uncertain, not to be relied on -- here, two candidate readings for one
#       year, neither ruled out
#
# surname|given|born|died|stone|conf|photo
Papic|Milka||1922|marble plaque, OBITELJ PAPIC, mounted on the Stipanic family monument; birth year read on site as either 1822 or 1870, the two not distinguished|?|phone photo, sent in chat 29 Sep 2026
Papic|Nikola|1868|1942|same plaque as Milka|p|phone photo, sent in chat 29 Sep 2026
Papic|Antonija|1882|1956|same plaque; given name's first letter is worn and unclear, read as Antonija|p|phone photo, sent in chat 29 Sep 2026
